{
  "unit": {
    "id": "5",
    "title": "What I like",
    "blurb": "mihi placet / mihi placent",
    "intro": "Latin does not say 'I like bread'. It says 'bread is pleasing to me': _mihi placet pānis_. The thing you like is the subject (nominative), and the person is in the dative (_mihi_ = to me, _tibi_ = to you). So the verb agrees with the thing: _placet_ for one (or something uncountable), _placent_ for several: _mihi placent ōva_ (I like eggs)."
  },
